-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/dea2c677-4a99-4425-bbde-9bbd66213622
-- title:
--   Eq. (26): estimate of the cross term
-- statement:
--   Let $\varphi\in(1,\phi]$, $\lambda_0>0$, $\bar\lambda>0$, and let $(z^k),(\bar z^k),(\lambda_k),(\theta_k)$ be generated by Algorithm 1 (EGRAAL) from any $z^0,z^1\in\mathcal E$, for some $g$ with domain $D$ and some $F$.
--   Then for every $k\ge1$,
--   $$2\lambda_k\langle F(z^k)-F(z^{k-1}),\,z^k-z^{k+1}\rangle\ \le\ \frac{\theta_k}{2}\|z^{k+1}-z^k\|^2+\frac{\theta_{k-1}}{2}\|z^k-z^{k-1}\|^2 .$$
--
--   The paper derives it from (18) via $2\lambda_k\|F(z^k)-F(z^{k-1})\|\|z^k-z^{k+1}\|\le\sqrt{\theta_k\theta_{k-1}}\|z^k-z^{k-1}\|\|z^k-z^{k+1}\|$; it turns (25) into the energy inequality (27).
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: the standing assumptions of §2.1: (C1)–(C3) and F locally Lipschitz → only the run and φ ∈ (1, ϕ], λ₀ > 0, λ̄ > 0; no (C1)–(C3) or Lipschitz assumption; reason: the estimate follows from (18) alone; the paper's setting is a special case
--   - encoding: g : E → (−∞, +∞] proper convex lsc → a set D with real values g : E → ℝ; D nonempty, ConvexOn ℝ D g, and the extension by +∞ off D lower semicontinuous (IsProperConvexLsc); reason: every proper convex lsc g is of this form (D = dom g) and conversely; same instances
--   - generalization: F : dom g → E; inputs z⁰, z¹ at which F is evaluated in (15), (17) → F : E → E, with monotonicity (and local Lipschitz continuity, where assumed) imposed on D only and values off D unconstrained; z 0, z 1 ∈ E arbitrary; reason: specializes to the paper by taking z⁰, z¹ ∈ dom g and any extension of F off dom g; for k ≥ 2 the iterates lie in dom g
--   - encoding: convention 0/0 = +∞ in (15) → egraalStep omits the middle entry of the minimum when F(z^k) = F(z^{k−1}); reason: the middle entry is then a/0 with a ≥ 0, i.e. +∞, and drops out of the minimum; same stepsizes
--   - encoding: z^{k+1} = prox_{λ_k g}(z̄^k − λ_k F(z^k)) with prox a function → IsProx D (λ_k g) (z̄^k − λ_k F(z^k)) (z^{k+1}): z^{k+1} ∈ D minimizes λ_k g(x) + ½‖x − w‖² over D; reason: under (C2) in finite dimension the minimizer exists and is unique, so the predicate determines the same iterates
--   - reading: index k unspecified (the algorithm runs for k ≥ 1) → every k ≥ 1; reason: every term is defined for k ≥ 1 (λ_{k−1}, θ_{k−1}, z^{k−1}); the paper uses the estimate for k ≥ 1
--   - encoding: the chain a ≤ b ≤ c ≤ d of (26) → the outer inequality a ≤ d; reason: the middle expressions are steps of the derivation; the chain's content is its outer inequality
-- source:
--   Malitsky, Golden Ratio Algorithms for Variational Inequalities, preprint (2018), proof of Theorem 2, p. 7, eq. (26)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_IsEGRAALRun

namespace GoldenRatioVI

/-- **Estimate (26) of the cross term.**
Malitsky, *Golden Ratio Algorithms for Variational Inequalities*, preprint (2018), proof of Theorem 2, p. 7, eq. (26): "Using (18), the rightmost term in (25) can be
estimated as 2λk⟨F(zk) − F(zk−1), zk − zk+1⟩ ≤ 2λk‖F(zk) − F(zk−1)‖‖zk − zk+1‖
≤ √(θkθk−1)‖zk − zk−1‖‖zk − zk+1‖ ≤ θk/2‖zk+1 − zk‖² + θk−1/2‖zk − zk−1‖²."

For a run of Algorithm 1 with `1 < phi ≤ ϕ`, `lam0 > 0`, `lbar > 0`, and every `k ≥ 1`:
`2 lam k ⟪F(z k) − F(z (k−1)), z k − z (k+1)⟫ ≤ theta k/2 ‖z (k+1) − z k‖² + theta (k−1)/2 ‖z k − z (k−1)‖²`.

**Formalization Note.** The outer inequality of the chain is stated; the two middle expressions
are steps of its proof. -/
theorem eq_26_cross_term_bound {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {D : Set E} {g : E → ℝ} {F : E → E} {phi lam0 lbar : ℝ}
    {z zbar : ℕ → E} {lam theta : ℕ → ℝ}
    (hphi : 1 < phi) (hphiG : phi ≤ Real.goldenRatio) (hlam0 : 0 < lam0) (hlbar : 0 < lbar)
    (hrun : IsEGRAALRun D g F phi lam0 lbar z zbar lam theta) (k : ℕ) (hk : 1 ≤ k) :
    2 * lam k * inner ℝ (F (z k) - F (z (k - 1))) (z k - z (k + 1)) ≤
      theta k / 2 * ‖z (k + 1) - z k‖ ^ 2 + theta (k - 1) / 2 * ‖z k - z (k - 1)‖ ^ 2 := by sorry

end GoldenRatioVI
